                  %a{:href => "#relation_to_homotopy_colimits_geometric_realization"} Relation to homotopy colimits (geometric realization)
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            The notion of
            %em homotopy Kan fibration
            is the evident
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+theory"} homotopy-theoretic
            generalization (
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %mn ∞
                    %mo ,
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (\infty,1)
              \-
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/categorification"} categorification
            = succeed ":" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibration"} Kan fibration
            is a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
            (hence:
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+objects"} simplicial objects
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/internalization"} internal
            to
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Sets"} Sets
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/right+lifting+property"} right lifting property
            against
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            inclusions, so a homotopy Kan fibration is a morphism of
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} simplicial
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"}
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn ∞
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
              \-groupoids
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+spaces"}> simplicial spaces
            ”,
            = succeed ")" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bisimplicial+sets"} bisimplicial sets
            = succeed "-lifting" do
              %em homotopy
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"} horn
            inclusions.
          %p
            Just like
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kan+fibrations"} Kan fibrations
            serve as the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/fibrations"} fibrations
            in the
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/classical+model+structure+on+simplicial+sets"} classical model structure on simplicial sets
            = succeed "-structure" do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/model+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"}
                model
                = succeed "-category" do
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mn ∞
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+object+in+an+%28infinity%2C1%29-category"} simplicial
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/infinity-groupoids"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mn ∞
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \infty
                \-groupoids
          %h2#definition Definition
          %p
          #HomotopyKanFibration.num_defn
            %h6 Definition
            %p
              A morphism
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %msub
                      %mi f
                      %mo •
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace"} :
                    %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi X
                      %mo •
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %msub
                      %mi Y
                      %mo •
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} f_\bullet \,\colon\, X_\bullet \xrightarrow{\;} Y_\bullet
              is a
              %em homotopy Kan fibration
              if for all
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/positive+numbers"} positive numbers
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi n
                    %mo ∈
                    %msub
                      %mi ℕ
                      %mo +
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n \in \mathbb{N}_+
              and all
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 0
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi k
                    %mo ≤
                    %mi n
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 0 \leq k \leq n
              the induced map
            #eq:HomotopyTheoreticKanFibration.maruku-equation
              %span.maruku-eq-number (1)
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mover
                      %mo →
                      %mrow
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                        %mspace{:width => "thickmathspace"}
                    %mi X
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msubsup
                      %mi Λ
                      %mi k
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %munder
                      %mrow
                        %msup
                          %mo ×
                          %mi h
                      %mrow
                        %mi Y
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %msubsup
                          %mi Λ
                          %mi k
                          %mi n
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %mi Y
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                    %msup
                      %mi Δ
                      %mi n
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                    X(\Delta^n)
                    \\xrightarrow{\;\;}
                    X(\Lambda^n_k)
                    \\underset
                    { Y(\Lambda^n_k) }
                    {\times^h}
                    Y(\Delta^n)
            %p
              (into the
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/homotopy+fiber+product"} homotopy fiber product
              of the space of space of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horns"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mi n
                      %mo ,
                      %mi k
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,k)
                \-horns
              in
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
              with that of
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplex"}
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n
                \-simplices
              in
              = succeed ")" do
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi Y
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} Y
            %p
              is
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/surjective"} surjective
              on
              = succeed "," do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connected+components"} connected components
            %p
              hence in that for all solid homotopy-commutative squares as follows, there exists a dashed lift up to homotopy (with the left morphism being the
              = succeed "-inclusion" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/horn"}
                  %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}>
                    %semantics
                      %mrow
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                        %mi n
                        %mo ,
                        %mi k
                        %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} (n,k)
                  \-horn
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/simplicial+sets"} simplicial sets
              regarded as degree-wise
              = succeed "):" do
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/discrete+topological+spaces"} discrete topological spaces
